.\" halite-api(8)
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt HALITE-API 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm halite-api
.Nd the HTTP API service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Op Fl -flag Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves the HTTP API: authentication, the execution and event endpoints,
and the webhook receivers.
.Pp
It holds no fleet state of its own.
It is a client of
.Xr halite-hub 8 ,
authenticating to it with an operator certificate, so every job it
submits is authorized by the hub's own policy against the principal the
request authenticated as.
The policy file it reads is the hub's, and reading it here is how the API
answers a permission question without a round trip.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "account subcommand"
.It Cm serve
Run the HTTP API.
This is what the service unit runs.
.It Cm token Ar subcommand
Issued tokens:
.Cm list ,
.Cm show ,
.Cm revoke ,
.Cm prune .
.Fl -principal
revokes every token a principal holds rather than one named token.
.It Cm account Ar subcommand
Local accounts:
.Cm hash
produces a password hash for the account file, and
.Cm list
reads what is in it.
.It Cm doctor
Run the diagnostics of the specification's section 26.4 that apply to this
service.
Changes nothing, and starts no listener, so it is safe to run against a
service that is already running.
It checks that the configuration loads, that the three certificates this
service holds are valid and not near expiry \(em the one it presents to
callers, the operator certificate it presents to the hub, and the CA it
verifies the hub with \(em that the hub answers, and that nothing about
this build contradicts the host's FIPS mode.
Exits non-zero only on a failure, not on a warning.
.It Cm version
Print the build identity.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--config path"
.It Fl -help
Describe the program without running the command.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Configuration file.
Defaults to
.Pa api.yaml
under the configuration root.
.It Fl -root Ar dir
Configuration root.
.It Fl -out Ar format
.Sy nested
(default),
.Sy json ,
.Sy yaml ,
or
.Sy txt .
.El
.Pp
.Cm serve
takes the listener, the TLS material, the hub it is a client of and the
identity it presents; see
.Nm
.Fl -help .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/halite/api.yaml" -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/halite/api.yaml
Configuration on the BSDs.
.It Pa /etc/halite/api.yaml
Configuration elsewhere.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/halite/pki
The operator certificate and key this service presents to the hub.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Produce a password hash for the local account file:
.Pp
.Dl halite-api account hash
.Pp
Revoke every token a principal holds:
.Pp
.Dl halite-api token revoke --principal cert:CN=ed
.Pp
Ask this service what is wrong with it:
.Pp
.Dl halite-api doctor
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halite-hub 8 ,
.Xr halite-node 8
.Pp
The policy this service enforces is the hub's:
.Nm halite-hub Cm policy show
reads the same file.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Ed Silva Aq Mt ed@edlitmus.info
